# lf127, the wheat-price map keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf127
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_rook_wheatfield
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the wheat-price map keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk always_knows_the_price_of_wheat
likes warm_bread old_tales old_maps summer_evenings
dislikes crowds drizzle
fears a_bad_harvest_with_no_bread_to_share another_thief_crossing_the_farm_gate
hopes a_full_granary_for_the_house a_fair_wheat_price_next_season
topics work +0.5 prices +0.4 family +0.3 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=generous gossip=curious refuse=plain tease=warm
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# runs the #farm#, knows the day's #wheat# #price#, shares #bread# freely, and keeps an old #map# whose #roads# are wrong.

words
oath! = Wheat and warm bread | By the good field
saying! = Know the price before filling the cart | A wrong road can still lead home
farm = farm | Longmead farm
field = field | wheat field
fields = fields | open fields
granary = granary | dry granary
barn = barn | farm barn
wheat = wheat | harvest wheat
grain = grain | stored grain
barley = barley | field barley
seed = seed | saved seed
seeds = seeds | saved seeds
sack = sack | grain sack
sacks = sacks | full sacks
bin = bin | grain bin
bins = bins | grain bins
stack = stack | covered stack
stacks = stacks | covered stacks
sheaf = sheaf | bound sheaf
sheaves = sheaves | bound sheaves
harvest = harvest | wheat harvest
plough = plough | field plough
furrow = furrow | straight furrow
soil = soil | good soil
rain = rain | needed rain
drizzzle = drizzle | thin drizzle
sun = sun | summer sun
summer = summer | long summer
evening = evening | long evening
morning = morning | early morning
night = night | quiet night
day = day | working day
hour = hour | late hour
cart = cart | grain cart
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
road = road | field road
roads = roads | drawn roads
path = path | farm path
bridge = bridge | stone bridge
map = map | old map
maps = maps | old maps
ink = ink | faded ink
mark = mark | map mark
marks = marks | map marks
town = town | near town
city = city | far city
market = market | busy market
price = price | wheat price
prices = prices | market prices
coin = coin | saved coin
wage = wage | fair wage
merchant = merchant | grain merchant
buyer = buyer | grain buyer
seller = seller | market seller
crowd = crowd | market crowd
crowds = crowds | market crowds
watch = watch | town watch
thief = thief | unknown thief
thieves = thieves | passing thieves
gate = gate | farm gate
fence = fence | field fence
hand = hand | farm hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | farm work
home = home | farmhouse
house = house | farm house
door = door | front door
window = window | front window
roof = roof | sound roof
larder = larder | home larder
table = table | family table
plate = plate | supper plate
plates = plates | supper plates
bread = bread | warm bread
loaf = loaf | fresh loaf
loaves = loaves | fresh loaves
meal = meal | evening meal
friend = friend | close friend
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
stranger = stranger | hungry stranger
family = family | farm family
child = child | young child
tale = tale | old tale
tales = tales | old tales
story = story | familiar story
stories = stories | familiar stories
festival = festival | town festival
bench = bench | wooden bench
cost = cost | wagon cost
leg = leg | aching leg
book = book | farm book
mornings = mornings | clear mornings
forge = forge | smithy forge
rope = rope | binding rope
storm = storm | passing storm
drizzle = drizzle | thin drizzle
tables = tables | long tables
latch = latch | gate latch
tracks = tracks | faint tracks
pace = pace | steady pace

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The #city# has too many faces and too little room for a good #cart#. | I would rather bargain at our #market#.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A hungry #neighbour# can have #bread# before anyone asks about #coin#. | A town should manage that much.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : The #festival# brings the whole #town# out to talk. | The #tales# reach me while I set the supper #plates#.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A new #hand# who pulls a #cart# can find #work# here. | I ask what they know and show the rest.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A #stranger# at my #gate# may need a #plate# before directions. | I keep a spare #loaf#.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The #watch# did not find the #thief# who crossed my #field#. | I still count my #sacks# myself.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : The #merchant# knows the #wagon# #cost#. | I know the #wheat# #price# before they speak.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# brings buyers to the #farm#. | My old #map# puts its #bridge# in the wrong place.
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #wheat# #price# changed this #morning#. | #greet#. There is #bread# at the #house#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Come eat before we count the #sacks#. | I found another fault in my #map#.
line @1 greet.return : The #wheat# has held its #price# since you left. | The #cart# has not yet left since your last visit.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : The #table# is ready if you are hungry. | I saved a place by the #window#.
line @1 again.open : I was tracing this #road# on the #map#. | Has the latest #wheat# #price# reached you?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Take a #loaf# for the #road#. | I must check the #granary#.
line @1 farewell.return : Another #tale# will be waiting. | The #wheat# may cost differently next time.
line @1 react.news : Speak while I close this #bin#. | Was it near the #market#?
line @1 react.news.new : I have not heard it at the #farm#. | Who brought this along the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : A #buyer# gave me a rough account. | You have filled a turn in the #story#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : The #sack# count might settle that claim. | Does the #market# #price# bear that out?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Sit and have #bread#. | The #work# can wait until you are ready.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I will bring out a fresh #loaf# for that. | There will be room at our #table#.
line @1 answer.how : Our #harvest# held, and the #family# has eaten. | My #leg# aches only a little today.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am checking the #wheat# in this #bin#. | Let me finish the #cart# count.
line @1 ask.how : Have you eaten on the #road#? | Did you see the #market# #price#?
line @1 sympathise : Come under the #roof# and eat first. | I have an old #tale# if company helps.
line @1 reassure : We can find another #path# on the #map#. | There will be #bread# for supper.
line @1 decline : I cannot sell the #seed# set aside for planting. | The #gate# stays locked after theft.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair enough. The #sacks# can remain in the #granary#. | Then we will speak after #harvest#.
line @1 thank : You helped turn the #cart# at the #gate#. | I was glad to share that #loaf#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The #bread# was on the #table# already. | I had that #map# open for my own use.
line @1 preclose : I must check the #bins# before #night#. | The #family# will be at the #table# soon.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your directions follow my old #map# too closely. | You know the #wheat# #price# from last season.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #grain# is dry. | #bc_fair_enough#. Another look at the #map# may help.
line @1 give.advice : Save a #sack# of #seed# before pricing the #harvest#. | Ask who drew the #road# on any old #map#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep company with the #wagon# as you travel. | Tell the #watch# if you see a strange #cart#.
scene wheat_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I know the #wheat# #price# before breakfast. | The #price# decides whether to send a #cart# to #market#.
b : Do you write it down? | Who brings the news?
a : In the #book#. | A buyer or a #hand#.

scene market_tally
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #merchant# counts #sacks# while I count #wages# and #seed#. | A fair #price# must leave room for both.
b : Does it ever? | Do you bargain long?
a : In a good #harvest#. | Until the sums agree.

scene saved_seed
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put the best #seed# aside before selling any #wheat#. | A full #wagon# means little without next season of planting.
b : Do you choose it yourself? | Where is it kept?
a : With another #hand#. | In the dry #bin#.

scene granary_bins
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #granary# #bins# need air around the lower #sacks#. | I check them after every #rain#.
b : Do they stay dry? | Who helps?
a : Under this #roof#. | The farm #hands#.

scene straight_furrow
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A straight #furrow# keeps the #plough# moving when the #field# is long. | I walk the first line before we begin.
b : Can you see the end? | Does the soil vary?
a : On clear #mornings#. | Near the #fence#.

scene cart_axle
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I look at the #wheel# before loading a full #cart#. | A broken one costs the #market# #day#.
b : Have you lost a load? | Can you mend it?
a : Not this season. | With the smith at the #forge#.

scene covered_stack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #stack# can shed #rain# if its top is properly tied. | I check the #rope# before a #storm#.
b : Does it hold? | What if it leaks?
a : Most times. | We move the #sheaves#.

scene wrong_bridge
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My old #map# draws the #bridge# upstream of its true place. | I leave the error there to remind me to look up.
b : Did you draw it? | Do you still use it?
a : A former owner did. | For the #roads# that remain.

scene map_ink
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #ink# on one old #road# has faded almost away. | I can still follow it with a finger.
b : Where does it lead? | Have you walked it?
a : Toward the #field#. | Not the whole distance.

scene old_tale
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A good old #tale# changes a little each time it is told. | I listen for the part the teller still remembers clearly.
b : Do you tell many? | Which is your favorite?
a : At supper. | One about a wrong #road#.

scene warm_bread
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Warm #bread# at the #table# can draw the #family# in from the #field#. | I keep one #loaf# for a late #hand#.
b : Do you bake it? | Do they come late?
a : The baker does. | During #harvest#.

scene summer_evening
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A long #summer# #evening# lets me walk the #fields# after supper. | I see which #fence# needs work.
b : Do you rest then? | Does the light last?
a : When I return. | Long enough.

scene thin_drizzle
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Thin #drizzle# leaves a #cart# muddy without watering the #wheat# deeply. | I would rather have a steady #rain#.
b : Does it hurt the crop? | Do you keep working?
a : When it lingers. | Under a #roof#.

scene festival_tables
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #festival# brings every #neighbour# to the long #tables#. | I like hearing what grew in other #fields#.
b : Do you trade stories? | Do you stay late?
a : A few #tales#. | Until the #family# is ready.

scene farmhouse_meal
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Our #house# serves whoever helped with the #harvest# that #day#. | I count #plates# before the #sacks#.
b : Do you have enough? | Who cooks?
a : I make sure. | We share it.

scene thief_at_gate
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #thief# crossed our #gate# and the #watch# found no one. | I have checked the #latch# myself since.
b : What was taken? | Did you see them?
a : A little #grain#. | Only their #tracks#.

scene new_hand
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Following one #furrow# teaches a fresh #hand# the #field#. | I give them a steady #pace# before a full #cart#.
b : Do they stay? | Who teaches them?
a : Some do. | I do when I can.

scene road_map
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The real #road# bends where my old #map# draws a straight line. | I have walked that bend often enough to know.
b : Does that bother you? | Will you correct it?
a : It amuses me. | Not yet.

story wrong_map [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I followed an old #map# toward a #bridge# it placed too near the #field#.
  : The real #bridge# stood farther down the #road#.
  ask : Did you keep the map?
  b : A useful mistake.
  : It still sits by my #window#.

story thief_night [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : Someone crossed the #farm# #gate# and took a little #grain#.
  : The #watch# came later and found no #tracks# they could use.
  ask : Did it happen again?
  b : That would anger me.
  : I repaired the #latch# and kept count.

story market_price [topic=prices self.age>=18]
  : A #buyer# offered the previous #price# for the present #wheat#.
  : I showed the #seed# and #wages# in my count.
  ask : Did they agree?
  b : An honest calculation.
  : After another #hour# at the #table#.

rule @bark_wheat
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #wheat# #price# rose today. | Count the #sacks# before loading.

rule @bark_map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say That #bridge# is drawn wrong. | The #road# bends beyond the #field#.

rule @bark_bread
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say There is #bread# at the #house#. | Set another #plate# on the #table#.

rule @bark_cart
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #cart# #wheel# needs checking. | Leave the #seed# #sack# here.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have the #wheat# #price# for today. | #greet#. Come inside for #bread#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : The #map# still puts that #bridge# wrong. | The #cart# is still being loaded on your return.
dlg @1 resident.job : I farm #self.workplace# and keep its #granary#. | I count #seed#, #sacks#, #wages#, and #market# #prices#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Take a #loaf# if you need one. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind the #gate#.
graft resident.hub
choice What is wheat worth today? -> price
node price
say I know the #market# #price#, but first I keep enough #seed# for our #field#.
free
choice Why keep a wrong map? -> map
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node map
say Its errors make me look up at the real #road#.
choice Back to the farm. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #grain# is dry. | #greet#. I have another old #tale#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #family# is waiting for supper. | I will check the #bins# tomorrow.
